# Where the @falese scope resolves from (ADR-084).
#
# The manifest declares plain semver ranges — never a `file:` path — so the
# lane is chosen here rather than baked into package.json. That is what makes
# one lockfile work in both lanes (ADR-084 §5).
#
# HOSTED (this default): GitHub Packages. It needs a token even for public
# packages, and a token must never live in this file — it is committed. Put it
# in ~/.npmrc or the environment instead:
#
#   //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
#
# OFFLINE: the static mirror baked into the CLI image, for an agent working in
# a sandbox with no live registry. Override with an environment variable, which
# outranks this file:
#
#   npm_config_@falese:registry=http://127.0.0.1:4873 npm ci
#
# It must be the environment, not another .npmrc — npm resolves
# CLI flag > env > *this file* > ~/.npmrc > global, so a user-level .npmrc
# would silently lose to this one.
#
# Yours to edit: repoint the scope at a proxy or internal registry and
# regeneration will not overwrite it.
@falese:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
